# What `COPY . .` must not drag into the build.
#
# The droplet builds the image on its own disk, so every megabyte of context
# is a megabyte of layer it has to store. Nothing here is read by `npm run
# build`: the React build needs package.json, craco.config.js, src/, public/,
# scripts/ and nginx.conf, and that is all.

# ── Version control and CI ──
.git
.gitignore
.github

# ── Installed and generated ──
node_modules
build
coverage
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ── Source map data for the eruv pages ──
# Raw exports kept for provenance and re-generation. The parsed output lives
# in src/data/, which is what the app imports.
*.kml
*.geojson
The Edgware Eruv & Surrounding Eruvin.json

# ── Tooling that runs on the host, not in the image ──
# build_race_data.py is run by the deploy script before `docker compose build`
# and writes src/data/race_data.json, which does get copied.
backend_tools

# ── Docs and scratch ──
*.md
*.code-workspace
__pycache__
*.pyc
.DS_Store
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
